"/farmland-atlas/kansas/sherman-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sherman County","/arc-plc/kansas/sherman-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Sherman County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids, February to March came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids got 16% of normal in March to April and 38% in February to March. Grid 23212 had its driest year in 1954 at 43% of normal.</p>"}
